finding: Re-review 33b88804..f8c95893: all three a00bfcce reproductions are repaired, but two paths still fail the public hook/restore claim. (1) The blanket restore guard rejects a legitimate in-tree SpritePlugin observer. Reproducer: build openGpuApp({defaults:false,plugins:[SpritePlugin]}); create an entity with Transform, MeshInstance and MeshMaterial; snapshot; remove MeshInstance/MeshMaterial, add Sprite, step(0) so the sprite publishes its generated mesh/material; restore the earlier image. Sprite's false notification deletes its cached instance and calls world.remove(eid,MeshMaterial), throwing World.remove: refuses "MeshMaterial" ... while restore notifies. This is the real unmodified SpritePlugin on a GPU-backed app, not merely a matching callback; /tmp/membership-sprite-gpu.ts reproduces with bun --preload /tmp/membership-gpu-preload.ts /tmp/membership-sprite-gpu.ts. Restore's guard must stay truthful, but the in-tree cleanup/recovery needs to coexist with it. (2) A table-attachment throw during restore still aborts the current membership's reconciliation before remaining tables and any observers run. Bind C to two GPU tables; add C, snapshot, remove C; fault-inject a throw in the first table's attachComponent and restore. C is present again, both tables have rowIndex=-1, and its observer received no attachment. Restore the same image again after removing the fault: no bit changed, so neither tables nor observer ever reconcile. Other changed bits and recovery participants now continue correctly, but this membership is permanently left behind. /tmp/membership-restore-gpu-table.ts reproduces against actual GpuTables with an injected attach error; /tmp/membership-restore-table.ts is its CPU binding-level differential. Table attachment occurs before the RESTORE beginChange/notification try. No successful notifying path was found bypassing the stack; the issue is the throw preventing notification altogether. The three earlier reproducers now show truthful guarded restore notifications, later-eid reconciliation, and no early same-eid reuse during nested destroy. Companion/side-effect balance probes still pass. ECS 131/131, named observer set 14/14, physics common/ECS-bridge 436/436 pass. Cost: 21 alternating rounds per runtime, each process last 21 of 121 fresh 10k-entity worlds, with pgrep -f 'bun test' gate before and during each process; interrupted round discarded. Start 2026-10-26 11:50:14 load 11.62/22.33/29.22; end 11:52:06 load 14.34/20.67/27.77; no matching test processes at either endpoint. Apple M4 Max, Bun 1.4.3 and Node 26.12.0. Median process-median milliseconds base->HEAD: JSC no requirement 1.410->1.631, requirement 2.067->2.295; V8 no requirement 3.267->3.605, requirement 4.280->5.543. Median paired HEAD/base ratios: JSC 1.199 and 1.148 (slower in 18/21 and 17/21 pairs); V8 1.022 and 1.028 (14/21 and 13/21). This run supports modest JSC overhead, not strict within-noise equivalence; V8 differences remain noisy. Harness, load samples and all per-round medians: /tmp/membership-final-ab.py and /tmp/membership-final-ab.json. No tracked files edited.
